diff --git a/DEPLOY.md b/DEPLOY.md
index 9536248..6438a75 100644
--- a/DEPLOY.md
+++ b/DEPLOY.md
@@ -200,3 +200,55 @@ subscriptions are untouched.**
   WhatsApp** to share, and a one-tap **📘 Send brochure** button on every CRM lead.
   It seeded itself from the app's live pack prices — give it one read and tweak any wording
   you want.
+
+---
+
+## 3 August 2026 — staff logins and the kitchen screen (Phase A)
+
+The app used to be all-or-nothing: anyone who could sign in could change a price or delete a
+subscription. Now each person gets their own login, and staff see a separate, much smaller
+screen built for the shift. **Additive again — the two new tables create themselves on first
+load, and no existing data is touched.**
+
+### Deploying it (same 2 steps, plus one restart)
+1. On PythonAnywhere → **Bash**: `cd oggainz-os && git pull`
+2. **Web → Reload** (this is what picks up the Python changes — a template edit alone would
+   not need it, but this update changes Python)
+
+Nothing new to set in the WSGI file. `OG_PASSWORD` and `OG_TEAM_PASSWORD` work exactly as
+before.
+
+### Setting Subramani up (2 minutes, do it once)
+1. **More → Staff & access**
+2. *Add someone*: name, role **Kitchen & delivery**, screen language **English or தமிழ்**,
+   and a 4–6 digit PIN. Add his phone number if you like.
+3. Tell him the PIN yourself. It is stored scrambled — nobody, including that page, can read
+   it back. If he forgets it, set a new one from the same page.
+4. Send him `https://oggainz.pythonanywhere.com/login` — he taps his name, types the PIN, and
+   lands straight on the kitchen screen.
+
+### What he sees
+Three tabs, and nothing else in the whole app:
+- **Orders** — tonight's list, tap ✓ Delivered or Skipped, tap a name for the full card
+  (what goes in the box, address, map, call, WhatsApp, meals remaining, a note field)
+- **Prep** — the batch quantities for the slot, tapped off one line at a time
+- **Run** — the riding order with ETAs, one tap per stop, and the whole route in Google Maps
+
+### What he cannot see or do
+No price, no revenue, no payment status — those screens have no money on them at all, so
+there is nothing to leak. He cannot create, edit, pause, renew or delete a subscription,
+cannot touch the menu, brochure, settings, exports, backups, CRM or invoices, and cannot
+change any day other than today. Every page in the app is refused to him unless it is on an
+explicit list, so a page added next month is locked until it is unlocked on purpose.
+
+### Keeping an eye on it
+- **More → Activity log** — who marked what delivered, what note they wrote, when they signed
+  in. Also shown at the bottom of the Staff page.
+- **More → Kitchen screen** opens exactly what he sees, from your own login.
+- Someone leaving: **Remove access** on the Staff page. Their history stays in the log.
+- Five wrong PINs in a row locks that account for 15 minutes (the login page is on the public
+  internet and 4 digits is not many guesses). Resetting the PIN unlocks it immediately.
+
+### Before deploying, if you changed anything
+`python test_permissions.py` — 88 checks that staff can reach their screens and nothing else.
+It copies the database to a throwaway file first, so it can never touch your real data.
